-- title:
--   Sections avoiding the zeroth branch meet only the component inl 1
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p hpN₀` for level $N_0p$ over `DRLevel.R p`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O :$ `DRLevel.R p` $\to O$ a ring homomorphism, and suppose the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Let $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved package `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ p 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`, so in particular a scheme $Y$ proper, flat and integral over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ together with a proper morphism $\mathrm{toDR} : Y \to \mathfrak X \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,R} \operatorname{Spec} O$ over $\operatorname{Spec} O$, and a family of invertible ideal sheaf data $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,v$ indexed by `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`, whose product is the ideal generated by $p$ on every affine open. Let $t : \operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ satisfy $t \circ \mathrm{toBase}$ (in diagrammatic order $t \gg \mathrm{toBase}$) $= \mathrm{id}$, i.e. a section, and assume that the image of the closed point of $O$ under $t$ followed by $\mathrm{toDR}$ does not lie in the set-theoretic range of the morphism $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\,0$ followed by `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`. Then $t$ of the closed point of $O$ lies in the support of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,(\mathrm{Sum.inl}\,1)$ and in the support of no other component $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,w$, $w \neq \mathrm{Sum.inl}\,1$.
--
--   This is the component-identification step for sections of the regular model of $X_0(N_0p)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: the two indices $\mathrm{Sum.inl}\,0$ and $\mathrm{Sum.inl}\,1$ correspond to the two strict transforms of the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre and the indices $\mathrm{Sum.inr}\,(n,i)$ to the exceptional chains above the nodes, and avoiding the branch cut out by $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O)\,0$ pins the reduction of the section onto the other strict transform. It is used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_sections_multidegree_eq_depth_of_exists_schemeHomOver_of_branch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_sections_multidegree_eq_depth_of_exists_schemeHomOver_of_branch).
